WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.240
- [Mark] All right. Ernesto.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.860
Ernesto. Where are you from originally?

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.810
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.283
- Yeah, I grew up in
South Central or South LA.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.313
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:10.313 --> 00:00:12.400
Did you have both your
parents when you were young?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.230
- No, I don't know my dad,

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.223
my mom was a sole provider.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.610
I was raised by my grandmother, basically.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.660
And that was solely because my mother

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.810
had to always be at work.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.523
She had to be at work for
like six in the morning.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.110
So she would leave at
4:30 to get there on time

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.510
and then when she got home
it was usually after dark.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.090
So my grandmother basically
saw me up to school

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.050
and received me when I came home.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.743
- [Mark] How would you
describe your childhood?

00:00:43.823 --> 00:00:46.823
- I was sheltered for
most of my childhood.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.483
I was sheltered, so I was a naive.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.470
Now, I would look out the window

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:57.940
see all the kids in the
neighborhood playing

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.260
and I'd ask my mom, "Can I go play?"

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.860
She'd tell me "No.", but
she never gave me a reason.

00:01:05.736 --> 00:01:09.670
I was the only child then.
And my mother's only child.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.180
So I don't know if that
had anything to do with it,

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.560
but I was sheltered.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.760
She was over protective.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.950
- [Mark] And you've been married before?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:19.853
- No.

00:01:19.853 --> 00:01:20.686
- [Mark] No kids?

00:01:20.686 --> 00:01:21.519
- No.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.730
- [Mark] So you'd like to go down to some

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.290
of the neighborhoods and
pick up some of the girls

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.170
that worked the streets.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.140
- Yes.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.753
- [Mark] How long has that been going on?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.763
- Off and on, I'd say maybe 15 years.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.143
20 closer to 20.

00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:44.070
- [Mark] And you'll take
the girls to a hotel

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.120
or motel?
- Yes. Yes.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:48.523
- [Mark] And you have regular girls

00:01:48.523 --> 00:01:51.003
that you frequent or you change it up?

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.170
- Well as they say, variety
is the spice of life, so.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.480
- [Mark] There's a lot to
choose from down there.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.420
- Oh yeah.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.680
That's why I couldn't understand.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.462
One thing that I couldn't
understand when I was young

00:02:03.462 --> 00:02:05.363
is you're supposed to marry one woman,

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.740
and still every woman has their
individual characteristics,

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.400
traits that are attractive.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.470
So it's hard to pick just one.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.250
- [Mark] Yeah. You do you go...

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.561
Which street do you
usually go to? - Figueroa.

00:02:21.561 --> 00:02:23.380
- [Mark] Figueroa. Yeah.
Figueroa has a huge selection

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.625
of beautiful ladies.

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:27.502
(nods head)

00:02:27.502 --> 00:02:28.980
There's something for everybody down there

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.770
and it's an interesting street 'cause like

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.450
after around 10, 11, like around midnight

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.370
you'll have cars lined up.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.203
- Yeah.

00:02:40.203 --> 00:02:41.036
- [Mark] Like so many cars lined up.

00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:42.380
- Like a drive through.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.250
- [Mark ] Yes. It looks like
a drive through and the...

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.843
So many girls, so many guys looking,

00:02:49.843 --> 00:02:52.120
I mean, I don't know how much,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.200
how many of the girls are actually getting

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.033
picked up-
- Right.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.860
- [Mark] but it's an
interesting phenomenon.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.250
- True.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:02.250
Some man just a drive around
just to see the women, I guess.

00:03:03.061 --> 00:03:04.150
- [Mark] Just look at them.
- Just to look at them.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.130
It's a turn on, I guess.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.573
Everyone has their own
vice or what have you.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.380
- [Mark] And what kind
of things have you seen?

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.080
You've had some crazy experiences?

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.570
- Yeah. I mean pretty much

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.153
everything from being robbed.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.530
Well, yeah, robbed basically.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.809
- [Mark] Yeah. Some of the
girls that's their specialties.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.830
- Yeah. And I don't know how she did it.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:37.103
Because maybe her feet or
something, I don't know.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.203
But yeah, it was odd.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.950
'Cause I had my money tucked in my shoe.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.880
So when I take my shoes off,
but she never got off the bed.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.050
So I don't understand how,

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:51.883
but hey.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:54.840
- [Mark] The girls are pros.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.673
- Yeah sure.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.800
- [Mark] You ever been arrested for...?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.960
- Yeah, I was arrested.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.060
I've been arrested for

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.493
burglary.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.950
- [Mark] But like not solicitation? - No.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.900
- [Mark] Nothing related to this? - No.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.363
That's possession. - [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:17.100
- No, but I'm just talking in terms of

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.550
the girls working the street.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.200
You enjoy the freedom?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.463
- Yeah definitely.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.190
I try relationships and
it's too much of a headache,

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.610
too many expectations once it's official.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:34.780
It's like, you have to do this,

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.813
you have to do that.

00:04:36.977 --> 00:04:40.000
And I guess you could
say I have an affinity

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.253
for non-conformity.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.970
I guess I don't like
to be told what to do.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.307
- [Mark] Yeah. - I mean-

00:04:47.307 --> 00:04:50.080
- [Mark] Are drugs are part of your life?

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.200
- Yeah. They were for awhile

00:04:58.473 --> 00:05:01.490
and I take a step back
sometimes 'cause I go so far

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.507
and I mess up so much money and I say,

00:05:04.507 --> 00:05:07.530
"okay, you got to get it together",

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.720
but then I'd stay clean.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.370
I've been through drug programs.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.743
Outpatient, inpatient, the whole deal.

00:05:17.371 --> 00:05:20.180
I mean obviously there
was a underlying issues

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.513
that they say

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.994
we take the drug.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.060
The drug is not the issue,

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.573
We take the drugs to resolve our issue.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:35.790
Whatever it may be.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.380
Whether it be forget
about it or cope with it

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.230
and deal with it.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.060
I think my main thing was
I didn't know my father

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.520
and I just couldn't understand how you...

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:54.540
Regardless of what the
situation or circumstance was

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.920
between you and my mother and
it has nothing to do with me.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.090
I'm your seed how could you not look for

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.163
your seed.

00:06:05.119 --> 00:06:09.580
So I don't know. I think that
probably played a big role

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:12.143
in me making some of my life choices.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.163
And like I said, my
mother was an only child,

00:06:17.495 --> 00:06:20.620
I don't have any aunts, uncles, cousins.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.420
I didn't have any
positive male role models

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.423
per se growing up.

00:06:27.957 --> 00:06:31.440
So yeah, once I got a taste
of freedom, it broke wide.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.840
So being out in the streets,

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:38.333
what's out in the streets,
pimps, players, hustlers, thugs.

00:06:39.668 --> 00:06:42.300
So those were like my male role models,

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.400
I guess you could say.

00:06:49.121 --> 00:06:50.050
- [Mark] So I mean you're...

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:53.560
Because of the childhood
experiences you had

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:57.660
the commitment of a marriage
or something like that

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.770
might not be your forte.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.243
- I mean I would like to be married.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.520
'Cause that's the ideal thing.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:11.273
Have a family and buy a
home and so forth and so on.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.470
I mean I would like to settle down.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.023
As part of the reason why
I don't have any children,

00:07:20.937 --> 00:07:21.880
everyone has their issues.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:22.713
No, one's perfect.

00:07:22.713 --> 00:07:24.270
Including myself, of course.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.240
And I don't think I've found anyone

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:29.180
to where even if we have our differences

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:30.980
she won't play pawn with my kids.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.190
You know, you can't see your son

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.170
because you want to have sex with me.

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:35.760
You can't see your daughter
because you won't give me money.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.310
Because that's important to me.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.540
Because my father wasn't there for me.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.440
So like the relationships I've been in,

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.520
they usually already have children.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.930
So I try to be a constant in their life.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.010
I tell them I'm not your father,

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:53.183
but you can still lean on
me, whatever it is you need.

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:57.800
An interesting part is
that I still keep in touch

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.480
with most of my exes children.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:01.380
I call them and wish them happy birthday

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.620
and they really appreciate it.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.840
They say, "wow my own
father doesn't call me

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:05.673
on my birthday."

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:10.730
And so that hits home
with me as far as kids,

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:11.723
children, whatever.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:17.250
So yeah, I mean I hope to be married.

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:18.190
- [Mark] Did you ever find yourself

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:21.030
developing stronger feelings
for any of the girls

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.293
that you pick up?

00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:23.283
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:23.283 --> 00:08:25.603
I'm genuinely a caring person.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:33.160
I try to befriend them,
I guess you could say.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.033
So it's not so much like
a business transaction.

00:08:37.445 --> 00:08:41.350
I think I'm just generally
concerned for people in general.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:45.870
So I try to get to know
them and see what led them

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.430
to pretty much like what they're doing.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:49.760
What led them to become a prostitute

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:54.760
and nine times out of
10, the constant variable

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.390
in their stories is that
they were abused at home

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.660
at a very early age by
whether it be a parent,

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.770
whether it be a relative or a neighbor

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:05.890
or whatever the case may be.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.450
- [Mark] It's pretty much
like a hundred percent

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.283
of the time?

00:09:08.283 --> 00:09:09.280
- Yeah. Pretty much.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.773
I mean, I've learned that over the years.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.410
Either they were abused or
abandoned, one of the two.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.770
So they were in foster care, foster system

00:09:21.002 --> 00:09:22.740
and nine times out of 10
you're gonna get abused

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.920
in the foster system.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:27.020
Whether it be physical
abuse, sexual abuse.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:30.700
It all plays a part especially
when you're at a young age,

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.533
it affects you.

00:09:31.533 --> 00:09:35.723
And if you don't get a
treatment for it, therapy,

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.310
it stays with you.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:41.143
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:44.600
I've interviewed a few hundred, I think

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.100
of these girls and it's
like sometimes your heart

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.310
just opens up and you wanna save them.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:50.143
You wanna help them.

00:09:50.143 --> 00:09:51.727
You wanna do something for them.

00:09:51.727 --> 00:09:53.620
And I don't know that.

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.860
I don't know that it's
even possible sometimes.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:59.793
- Yeah. I mean I try to be an optimist.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:04.240
Some of the stories that I've
heard from some of the women,

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.920
it's like it makes me feel like

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.400
I haven't gone through anything.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:09.667
When they tell me their stories it's like,

00:10:09.667 --> 00:10:13.560
"Wow, you really survived
that and you're still here

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.100
and you're still-
- They've been through a lot.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:16.502
- Yeah. They've been through a lot.

00:10:16.502 --> 00:10:17.480
I was like...

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.610
- [Mark] I think I'll be eternally hopeful

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:24.270
that someday I'll save
somebody or help somebody

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.640
in some way that makes a real difference

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.020
but they seem to be
resistant to it as well.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:33.410
It's almost like they're so
ingrained in this low self-worth

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.920
that this career requires.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.770
- True. I think once you...

00:10:44.268 --> 00:10:47.100
Once you've been through so much,

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.510
it's like one thing after another.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:51.270
It's like you expect that's
what you've come to expect.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.590
So why even try to pick myself up

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.540
when something negative
is gonna happen anyway

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.150
every time I do.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.173
Which has been my life story as well.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.620
Like when I tried to
run away from the drugs

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.410
and street life is like,

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:11.110
I'll take, I'll get a job,
I'll take two steps forward.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:14.400
And then something in life, a life hurdle,

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.380
I guess you would call
it, will make me stumble

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.210
and I'll fall back two steps.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.040
I'll take one step forward
and two steps back.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.970
As they say, you'll make progress in time.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.403
So it's like...

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.780
Well what's the sense
of continuing to try.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:29.613
And it's like...

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.230
And they say your life is predestined.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:36.410
You know I don't know how true that is.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:40.220
I think it has to do with
a lot of your choices,

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:44.030
within your choices come
from how you were raised

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:45.340
where you were raised.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.563
Your environment is
part of who you become.

00:11:53.808 --> 00:11:56.433
- [Mark] Yeah. What I suspect is the abuse

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.790
that we experienced as
children are like...

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:03.013
Let's take some of the girls
that work at the streets,

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.840
the abuse, the lack of
love, the disrespect

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:10.210
that they endured as
children become something

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:13.127
that they look for as adults.

00:12:13.127 --> 00:12:14.270
- They say it has a standard.

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:16.130
Because that's an interesting point

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:21.130
because I noticed when I try
to help, I guess you could say

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:26.330
to whatever extent, it's
like they push you away.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.020
If you're nice to them they pushed,

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.460
they don't want that.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:30.760
They don't know how to react to that

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:32.726
because no one's ever been.

00:12:32.726 --> 00:12:34.640
And so it's like...

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.220
I'm like "What's wrong?"

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.180
But I had to come to the realization that,

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.550
once you've been through so much

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.600
and then they've probably been tricked,

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.000
someone came to them and
in that fashion as an...

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.540
As if they were wanting to help them

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.920
and then it wound up being
something completely opposite.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:55.210
- [Mark] Well, I think that
the only thing that works

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.230
for an adult who's been abused as a child

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.870
is something very similar
to that relationship

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.900
that they were abused
in when they were young.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.710
So this working the streets

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:10.732
and being treated like
just being used by everyone

00:13:10.732 --> 00:13:13.650
does the trick nicely for them.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:15.640
That's my suspicion.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.960
